<!--
  SignPath artifact configuration for the AlphaCode Windows release archive.

  Upload this with the SignPath "Custom" artifact-configuration editor (paste
  the XML), or click "Upload an artifact sample" and feed it
  dist/alphacode-windows-x86_64.zip. SignPath will generate an equivalent
  configuration that you can replace with this file.

  Why the root element is <zip-file>: the release ships TWO Windows binaries,
  alphacode.exe (the CLI) and AlphaCode.Desktop.exe (the .NET/WPF GUI host).
  They must be Authenticode-signed. A ZIP root lets SignPath sign both in a
  single signing request, which is the shape the CI upload step produces
  (actions/upload-artifact@v4 stores a ZIP).

  Why an EXPLICIT name list instead of a wildcard: the previous layout shipped
  the GUI host *embedded inside* alphacode.exe (see
  docs/engineering/windows-av-false-positive.md). Naming both files exactly
  means a change that re-embeds, renames, or adds a third binary fails the
  signing request instead of silently signing the wrong thing. If that ever
  happens, update this file deliberately.

  hash-algorithm defaults to sha-256, which is what SmartScreen and modern
  Windows expect; it is left implicit on purpose.
-->
<artifact-configuration xmlns="http://signpath.io/artifact-configuration/v1">
  <zip-file>
    <pe-file path="alphacode.exe">
      <authenticode-sign/>
    </pe-file>
    <pe-file path="AlphaCode.Desktop.exe">
      <authenticode-sign/>
    </pe-file>
  </zip-file>
</artifact-configuration>
